
Recent CUDA 11.4 will not work with GCC releases past 10.0 so
we need this crap : 


C_oberon$ nvcc --version 
nvcc: NVIDIA (R) Cuda compiler driver
Copyright (c) 2005-2021 NVIDIA Corporation
Built on Mon_Oct_11_21:27:02_PDT_2021
Cuda compilation tools, release 11.4, V11.4.152
Build cuda_11.4.r11.4/compiler.30521435_0

C_oberon$ nvcc -ccbin g++-10 -I../include -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets -c -o index_hack.o index_hack.cu
C_oberon$ nvcc -ccbin g++-10 -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets -o index_hack index_hack.o -lgomp




----------------------------------- other foo

for multi-stream concurrency  

see https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/gpu-pro-tip-cuda-7-streams-simplify-concurrency/

$ nvcc --default-stream per-thread -ccbin g++-10 -I../include -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets -c -o index_hack.o index_hack.cu
$ nvcc --default-stream per-thread -ccbin g++-10 -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets -o index_hack index_hack.o -lgomp 
 
